Teleport for sure, create monster somewhat limited.
(I've written about those above.)

> Because you
> get a trainload of those.  (Wands of striking
> are also abundant, but I only consider them
> to be useful in the early game, unless you
> count polyfodder as a use.  Wands of
> digging are more arguable: some of them
> are useful, but I've never found a use for
> more than about a third of them.)

They are most useful as escape means (in games where
you are not playing a tank); it's always good to have
a couple. Later they can be convenient for the mazes,
since a pick-axe may require too many turns. For the
Plane of Earth you should also keep two (or three).

In my own games in the end I also often have more than
I need, but I've had games where they had been scarce.

